{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Let us make us a name.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): they sought to settle in one place, since they were joined together, and they found no place other than Shinar. Therefore they wanted to build themselves a city and a tower that would hold them all — the city for dwelling and the tower for a sign and a name, so that all the people of the world would see it and direct themselves toward it and settle in that city and not in any other place. This is the meaning of ״lest we be scattered,״ and therefore HaShem scattered them, because they came against His intention, which was that the nations should spread throughout the entire world and settle in all the places of the earth, for this is why He created it, as it says (Isaiah 45:18): ״ולשבת יצרה״ — 'and formed it to be inhabited.'" "<b>By way of the Midrash.</b> ״Let us make us a name״ — this is idolatry. It is written here ״ונעשה לנו שם״ and it is written there (Exodus 23:13) ״ושם אלהים אחרים לא תזכירו״ — just as there it refers to idolatry, so too here it refers to idolatry. And further, they interpreted in the Midrash Tehillim: ״הבה נבנה לנו עיר״ — הבה means counsel, as is said (Judges 20:7) ״הבו לכם דבר ועצה הלום״; and עיר means a deity, as is said (Daniel 4:7) ״ואלו עיר וקדיש״." "<b>And in the Midrash</b> of the Ten Commandments I saw that they said: Let us take axes and split the heavens, so that the waters will pour out, so that He not do to us as He did to the generation of the Flood; and let us make chunks out of the heavens, and wage war against the King who is in heaven. And in that tower there were seventy steps to the east and, opposite them, seventy steps to the west, and the Holy One, blessed be He, descended there with seventy angels and confounded their language and their speech — thus far. <b>Furthermore,</b> in Bereshit Rabbah they said: 'Not all of us — let the Most High choose for Himself; come, let us wage war against Him' — thus far." "<b>By way of reason (sekhel).</b> ״Let us make us a name״: the people of the dispersion were wicked, versed in all wisdom, and they built the city and the tower in order to save themselves from a flood of fire, because they had already seen the destruction of the world in a flood of water; they feared for their lives and needed to make a structure in a place where, if He wished to bring a flood of fire and burn the world, they would be saved from it and the fire would not come near their boundary. And this is the meaning of the war mentioned in the Midrash — that is, to act presumptuously against the supernal forces contrary to the will of the Holy One, blessed be He, and to bind a portion of the element of fire so that it would not be able to approach the city, just as we find even in our own generation certain sages who know the power to bind a portion of lightning [which is now known by the name (Donnerableiter), and a trace of this is also found in Tosefta Shabbat ch. 7] so that it does not come except within a known boundary. And there is yet another reason: since they saw that the Holy One, blessed be He, had decreed death upon the first man, and they saw themselves as possessed of tremendous strength and power, great in wisdom and in stature, and their lives were long and nothing was beyond their ability to do — yet behold, they are mortal, branches corrupted by the corruption of the root — therefore they devised a stratagem to build a structure and raise it on high to a certain measure in order to escape death. And for this reason HaShem scattered them, for they had plotted against the decree of the Holy One, blessed be He." "<b>Now behold,</b> the verses close the door upon the evil thoughts that they were thinking in their hearts and did not wish to make public. <b>And to</b> this matter they alluded in the Midrash when they said: ״ודברים אחדים אחודים״ — that is, closed off; the deeds of the generation of the Flood were explicitly stated, the deeds of the generation of the Dispersion were not explicitly stated — thus far. And I have heard that the builders of the tower were seventy, and there is no doubt that they had a known intention in this." "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah: 'let us make for ourselves a name' — their sin was the sin of their first father, who cut the shoots; so too these men cut the shoots and separated the fruit from the tree. This is what is meant by ונעשה לנו שם, in the language of the verse concerning the generation of Enosh, who were idolaters, in connection with which He mentioned שם, as it is said (Genesis 4): אז הוחל לקרא בשם ה׳ — and הוחל is from the language of חלול השם (profanation of the Name). So too He mentioned here וזה החלם לעשות, for that deed was a profanation of the Name. Or one may say that אז הוחל and החלם are from the language of התחלה (beginning), and one should not remove them from their plain sense, and the meaning in both cases is that they were making a beginning from the end, and this is the cutting (קצוץ). Therefore He used the language וזה החלם לעשות, that is, they make a beginning from the end, which is called זה, and is called שם, for thus they said: ונעשה לנו שם — this is the last measure, and they did not believe in anything above it, and in this they were cutting the shoots. Because of this it is said of them ויהי בנסעם מקדם, and our Rabbis, of blessed memory, interpreted: they uprooted themselves from the Ancient One of the world (מקדמונו של עולם). And in order to make clear that this sin of theirs was the sin of the first man, therefore He said: אשר בנו בני האדם." "<b>And they said</b> in the Midrash: בני האדם — what, sons of donkey-drivers, sons of camel-drivers? Rather: the sons of the first man (בנוי דאדם קדמאה). They hinted to us that they are sons resembling their first father in this sin. And from this you will not find in this parashah that He mentions the name Elohim as He mentioned it in the parashah of the Flood, for the generation of the Flood denied the last measure, and therefore they were destroyed from the lower earth and likewise from the upper by their banishment, and along with this they were blotted out from this world and the world to come." "<b>And behold,</b> this is measure for measure: they sinned against Elohim and the earth, which is from Elohim, was destroyed for them; but the generation of the Dispersion denied the special Name (השם המיוחד), and therefore He punished them with His great Name and showed them His power — and this is the language of וירד. Behold, each one was punished through that in which he sinned, and their punishment was measure for measure: just as they separated what was joined and unified, so the Holy One, blessed be He, separated their union and scattered them over the face of all the earth. And furthermore, because they devised an evil scheme through the wisdom within them: by the measurement of the tower's height it was known among them, as they upheld the honor of the icon (כבוד האיקונים) and denied the sovereignty. And all this was in Babylon. And you already know that when our holy sanctuary and our glory was destroyed and the sacred vessels were exiled there as well, there Nebuchadnezzar made the golden image called Bel, and this is what is said (Jeremiah 51): ופקדתי על בל בבבל, and this is what is said (Daniel 3): אקימה בבקעת דורא במדינת בבל — this is the valley mentioned here: וימצאו בקעה. And all this was a cleaving in unity and a cutting of the shoots, and may the Holy One, blessed be He, guard us from errors; may He teach us and guide us in His truth."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {1 "Rabbeinu Bahya cites the verse in Daniel as דניאל ד (Daniel 4); the reference Daniel 4:7 follows the chapter division of the printed Hebrew text.", 3 "The parenthetical (דאננעראבלייטער) is a Yiddish/German transliteration of 'Donnerableiter' (lightning conductor), evidently a later editorial gloss embedded in the text; the bracketed reference to Tosefta Shabbat ch. 7 is likewise editorial."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:12:04.620092774Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}